and this can be done by considering one couple of nodes at a time and run CI
tests, in order to remove edges. For example $A$ and $B$ are always dependent
one another because there is no separating set for them, so the edge between
them remains.

For $A$ and $D$ instead, we will have that

$ "CI"(A, D | B, C) = "True" $

so we have to remove the edge between them. Similar result for $B$ and $C$ that
are separated by $A$. So in the end we obtain the following skeleton

