      edge(A, "-", B)
      edge(A, "-", C)
      edge(B, "-", D)
      edge(C, "-", D)
    },
  ),
)

Once we have the skeleton, we need to give a orientation to the edges and this
can be partially done by finding colliders (because they are the only ones
identifiable from data). In this particular case, if we consider the triplet
$B$, $C$ and $D$, we have that $B$ and $C$ are not adjacent in the graph and $D$
is not in their separating set (before we saw that only $A$ is in their
separating set). So we can conclude that $D$ is collider.

