      node(B, [$B$])
      node(C, [$C$])
      node(D, [$D$])

      edge(A, "-", B)
      edge(A, "-", C)
      edge(B, "-|>", D)
      edge(C, "-|>", D)
    },
  ),
)

Since we already found all colliders, we can infer more orientations by applying
the *Meek rules*

#figure(
  image("images/meek_rules.png", width: 50%),
  caption: [ Meek Rules ],
)

that basically exploit the fact that there are no more colliders to be found,
otherwise we would have find them in the previous step. Hence, even though there
are possible configurations of inderected edges that could form a collider, they
cannot be in the true structure of the model, so they are discarded.

#figure(
